\title{Log powers}
\date{2026-10-23T13:53:05Z}
\tag{algorithms}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\taxon{Lemma}
\p{For any real numbers #{a,b > 1} and #{x > 1}, ##{a^{\log_x b} = b^{\log_x a}.}}

\proof{
Taking the #{\log_x} of both sides and simplifying yields ##{\log_x b \log_x a = \log_x a \log_x b} which is clearly true.
}
